{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>\u201cThe struggle itself toward the heights is enough to fill a human\u2019s heart. One must imagine Sisyphus happy.\u201d</i> \u2013 Albert Camus.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sisyphus, king of Corinth, has tricked the Gods and Death. To punish him, the Gods condemned him to push a boulder uphill forever, only for it to roll back each time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>But Sisyphus didn't give up. He decided to livestream it.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Imagine Sisyphus Happy is a fast-paced clicker + QTE game about life, spectacle, and finding meaning in repetition. Roll your boulder, pull off stunts, and try to make the eternal grind worth living.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Push the boulder. Do tricks. Go live.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Progressing from Greek myth to the modern day, the story asks two simple questions:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Aren\u2019t you a Sisyphus too?</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Can you Imagine Sisyphus Happy?</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Planned release \u2013 Q1 2026 \u2013 will have:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Many tricks and relatable modern scenes</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Large QTE variety, chains and combos</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A simulated streamer economy</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A shop with cosmetic upgrades</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The eternal grind split into short sessions</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There will be no in-game purchases.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3959020?t=1756873551","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3959020/edfc697dbf2f7fcf881ae5d7d66c4f30e94c3cee/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1756873551","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3959020/fdf1754f4aadff9c9e6fb9105b223c18796d49d7/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1756873551","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3959020/fdf1754f4aadff9c9e6fb9105b223c18796d49d7/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1756873551","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Color Alternatives","id":66},{"description":"Custom Volume Controls","id":68},{"description":"Adjustable Difficulty","id":78},{"description":"Save Anytime","id":79},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>\u201cThe struggle itself toward the heights is enough to fill a human\u2019s heart. One must imagine Sisyphus happy.\u201d</i> \u2013 Albert Camus.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sisyphus, king of Corinth, has tricked the Gods and Death. To punish him, the Gods condemned him to push a boulder uphill forever, only for it to roll back each time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>But Sisyphus didn't give up. He decided to livestream it.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Imagine Sisyphus Happy is a fast-paced clicker + QTE game about life, spectacle, and finding meaning in repetition. Roll your boulder, pull off stunts, and try to make the eternal grind worth living.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Push the boulder. Do tricks. Go live.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Progressing from Greek myth to the modern day, the story asks two simple questions:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Aren\u2019t you a Sisyphus too?</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Can you Imagine Sisyphus Happy?</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Planned release \u2013 Q1 2026 \u2013 will have:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Many tricks and relatable modern scenes</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Large QTE variety, chains and combos</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A simulated streamer economy</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A shop with cosmetic upgrades</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The eternal grind split into short sessions</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There will be no in-game purchases.</p>","developers":["UnplayTheGame"],"genres":[{"description":"Action","id":"1"},{"description":"Casual","id":"4"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Simulation","id":"28"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3959020/d3d61e218dfaf1f556d3da8236906198aa4743f4/header.jpg?t=1756873551","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Ubuntu 20.04 (or equivalent 64\u2011bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel i3\u20113220 / AMD FX\u20116300 or equivalent<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Intel HD 4000 or better</li></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> macOS 12 Monterey or newer<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Apple M1 or Intel with Metal support<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Apple Silicon GPU or any Metal\u2011capable Intel/AMD GPU<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 500 MB available space</li></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"movies":[{"highlight":true,"id":257192422,"mp4":{"480":"http://video.aka